From f8202526dfedf6a3b74bb093bfc85e4322f0be8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mesh-LLM CI <ci@mesh-llm.local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:45:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] skippy: propagate ctx_other for nemotron-h-moe MTP draft
 contexts

The llama_context constructor gates ctx_other propagation by arch.
A NextN-only nemotron-h-moe draft omits token_embd/output and borrows
the trunk tensors through ctx_other (see graph_mtp), but there was no
NEMOTRON_H_MOE clause, so the constructor silently dropped
params.ctx_other and graph_mtp asserted at reserve time with
'tok_embd_w != nullptr'.

Add the missing clause mirroring the INKLING one: gated on
LLAMA_CONTEXT_TYPE_MTP so trunk contexts of the same arch never adopt
a stray ctx_other.
---
 src/llama-context.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index f09531921..679da84c5 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -164,6 +164,16 @@ llama_context::llama_context(
         cparams.ctx_other = params.ctx_other;
     }
 
+    // A NextN-only nemotron-h-moe MTP draft omits token_embd/output and borrows
+    // the trunk tensors through ctx_other (see graph_mtp in nemotron-h-moe.cpp).
+    // Without this clause the constructor silently drops params.ctx_other and
+    // the draft context asserts at graph build time.
+    if (model.arch == LLM_ARCH_NEMOTRON_H_MOE &&
+            params.ctx_type == LLAMA_CONTEXT_TYPE_MTP &&
+            params.ctx_other != nullptr) {
+        cparams.ctx_other = params.ctx_other;
+    }
+
     // Initialize backend samplers here so they are part of the sampling graph
     // before the reserve passes run later in this function. This avoids a later
     // re-reserve when graph nodes change.
